Direwolf, a software "soundcard" AX.25 packet modem/TNC and APRS encoder/decoder,
by John Langner, WB2OSZ. GPL-2.0-or-later (see LICENSE and each file's header).

Upstream:  https://github.com/wb2osz/direwolf
Release:   1.8.1
Commit:    a231971a652bfb574a4bae9a5d875fbce53d2267 (tag 1.8.1, "Release 1.8.1", 2025-11-11)

The files under src/ are copied unmodified from that commit's src/ directory: the receive core
(demodulators, multi-slicer, HDLC, FX.25, IL2P), the transmit path (HDLC send, tone generator, FX.25
and IL2P send) and the headers they include. LICENSE is the upstream LICENSE file. SHA256SUMS lists
every vendored file, so the copy can be checked against the upstream tag:

  git clone --depth 1 --branch 1.8.1 https://github.com/wb2osz/direwolf
  cd direwolf && sha256sum -c <this directory>/SHA256SUMS

To move to a new release: copy the same files from it, update this file and SHA256SUMS, rebuild with
../../build.sh (the pinned Emscripten) and run the package tests.
